        <title type="html"><![CDATA[HTTP Cache-Control stale-if-error request]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39812</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39812"/>
        <updated>2025-06-06T00:14:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The Cache-Control directive <code class="notranslate">stale-if-error</code> is a request and response. The behaviour is documented as a response, but not as a request.</p>
<p dir="auto">The reason for this is that browsers don't seem to implement this in requests. Normally we wouldn't bother documenting this then, but it looks like an omission in docs because it is unsymmetric.</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds a note about what it should do and that it isn't supported - and points to browser compatibility for more information. The compat doesn't say anything, but if this is ever supported then it wil.<br>
I don't love this solution, but I think it is worth the note, since we did get an issue posted.</p>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #39674.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3089389467" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39674" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/39674/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39674">#39674</a></p>]]></content>
